meta {
  name: Anyone: the hub, signing in, and what the access body publishes
  seq: 1
}

docs {
  What Regulation (EU) 2025/327 requires an access body to publish: the Art. 58
  information duty, the Art. 57(1)(j) registers of permits and results (Art. 61(4)),
  and the Art. 59 activity report. Since #404 (ADR-044) every API route needs a
  session, so these are read signed in, with the collection's default session. Only requests 01 (is
  the hub up) and 06 (where to sign in) still go without one, because they are
  what makes signing in possible, and 08 and 09, the Klarbefund app's account
  creation, which answers only a verified App Attest attestation (ADR-054).
  The start page's TestFlight form (07, ADR-048) is gone (ADR-050).
}
